NAME
  webinstall - install Freax over the network from a stock OpenOS diskette

SYNOPSIS
  webinstall [OPTIONS]...

DESCRIPTION
  webinstall downloads the Freax operating system from a remote repository
  and installs it onto a formatted, writable hard drive. It is meant to run
  on a stock OpenOS diskette, so a Freax install medium is not required: boot
  OpenOS, attach an internet card and a target drive, fetch this script with
  wget, and run it with lua.

  webinstall reads the shipped-file list (manifest) from the repository,
  streams every file to the target in chunks (a file never has to fit in
  RAM), then generates the account database, labels the target, and sets the
  machine boot address. Files that are dev-only or machine-local
  (.gitignore, README.md, selfcheck.lua, /etc/passwd, /etc/shadow,
  /etc/hostname) are never downloaded.

  This program uses the OpenOS libraries (filesystem, component, internet,
  shell, term, computer) and does not run on Freax itself.

OPTIONS
  --source=URL
    Base URL of the Freax repository. The default is the upstream
    raw.githubusercontent.com mirror. Files are fetched from
    URL/<path-without-leading-slash>.

  --to=ADDR
    Install to the filesystem whose component address starts with ADDR.
    Without it, webinstall prompts when more than one writable target is
    attached.

  -y, --yes
    Do not ask for confirmation before writing to the target.

  --label=NAME
    Label to apply to the target filesystem. Default: freax.

  --nosetboot
    Do not set the target as the machine boot device.

  --noreboot
    Do not offer to reboot after installation.

  -h, --help
    Show usage and exit.

FILES
  /manifest
    Shipped-file list fetched from the repository and written to the target;
    it also drives install and the legacy apt sysupdate/sysupgrade path.

  /etc/passwd, /etc/shadow
    Generated on the target with a single root account (optionally with a
    password, hashed with the target's own lib/sha256.lua).

  /etc/hostname
    Written as freax on the target.

EXAMPLES
  Install from upstream, choosing the target interactively:
    wget -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Bufka2011/Freax/main/webinstall.lua /tmp/webinstall.lua
    lua /tmp/webinstall.lua

  Unattended install to a known drive:
    lua /tmp/webinstall.lua --to=12ab --yes

  Install from a mirror without touching the boot address:
    lua /tmp/webinstall.lua --source=http://192.168.1.5/freax --nosetboot

EXIT STATUS
  0 on success (or user cancellation), 1 on failure such as a missing
  internet card, no writable target, an incomplete download, or a failed
  verification.